    "info": {
      "name": "OTR Downstream Smoke Workflow (Composite + Upscale + Blend with per-stage save tees)",
      "description": "BUG-LOCAL-031 verification harness with explicit per-stage on-disk save tees. Five-node chain: VideoComposite -> SaveCopy(_smoke_composite) -> RTXUpscale -> SaveCopy(_smoke_upscale) -> PostUpscaleProcgenBlend(_smoke_blended). SaveCopy is a TEE: it copies the upstream mp4 to a sibling file with the suffix, then passes the ORIGINAL upstream path through unchanged so the next node operates on the canonical filename. After a run completes you get FIVE playable mp4s on disk: (1) composited/<ep>.mp4 (canonical composite output -- clobbered each smoke run), (2) composited/<ep>_smoke_composite.mp4 (preserved tee #1), (3) obs/<ep>.mp4 (canonical upscale output -- clobbered each smoke run), (4) obs/<ep>_smoke_upscale.mp4 (preserved tee #2), (5) obs/<ep>_smoke_blended.mp4 (final blend, suffix-protected). Each smoke run overwrites items #1, #3, #5 but #2 and #4 are stage-specific archives you can play side-by-side for QA. Skips Story / Director / Bark / Kokoro / MusicGen / AudioGen / FLUX / HuMo / LTX (all assets reused from prior run). Total runtime ~3 min. Edit Node 52 paths + Node 58 procgen path to retarget a different episode.",
      "version": "3.0",
      "purpose": "smoke-test-with-per-stage-save-tees"
    }
  },
  "version": 0.4
}
